    "title": "What goes into a professional brand book: a checklist for your business",
    "description": "A complete brand book includes much more than a logo. Use this checklist to evaluate your brand documentation.",
    "cover": "/assets/blog/brandbook-checklist/01_cover_19516-33758373_8106992.jpeg",
    "body": "Professional branding is a strategic document that defines rules for creating and using the visual identity of the company, and provides a tone of communication with the audience. Business is a kind of instruction that provides a sequence in all aspects of communication and helps the brand be recognizable and clear. In this article we'll see exactly what a professional brand has.\n\nThe first and most important part of the brand is mission, poetry and company values. These concepts form the base of a brand, explain why a company exists, what they want to achieve and what the principles of their business are. For example, a mission can reflect the social role of a brand while values define its ethics and approach to work.\n\nThe second chapter is the logo and the rules of use. In a brand, it's important to note what the logo looks like in different formats: color, monochrome, inversion. The minimum size of the logo, proportions, media placement rules and examples of no use allowed. It guarantees that the logo will look professional and similar in all materials.\n\nThe equally important component is the firms of a colored palette. It's made up of basic and extra colors that will be used in all of the visual communication of the brand. A brand defines accurate color values in various formats: CMYK, RGB, HEX and Pantone. This allows you to ensure the accuracy of color rendering independently of the medium type.\n\nFonts - another key element for a brand. Each brand selects a unique set of fonts that reflect its style. Usually define the primary font for headers, headers and text and alternative variants. Size, spacing between lines and use rules on different platforms.\n\nThe special attention should be taken into one of the heads -- the style of communication with the audience. A brand note shows the basic principles of writing texts, desired tone and approach to different target groups. For example, for a young brand, it could be a noisy and informal style, whereas for a law firm, it's reserved and official.\n\nIn addition to visual and text elements, a professional brand has to include examples of all the components in real terms. It could be credit cards, firm forms, packaging, printing pages for social networking and other media. Because of that, all partners and contractors can use brand elements correctly without explanation.\n\nIt's also worth mentioning the adaptability of a brand. The designed document should take effect in the development of the company, the extension of the equipment or the exit of new markets. For example, if a brand is planning an international expansion, a brand should already have multilingual content or a logo adaptation rule.\n\nBrandabk is not just a set of rules, but a foundation to build a strong and recognizable brand. By investing in its creation, the company puts the foundation for long-term success. Thanks to the brand, you can keep the wholeness of your image, efficiently communicate with customers and remain competitive in the dynamic world of business."
