    "cover": "/assets/blog/brandbook-for-startup/01_cover_1709293966603.jpeg",
    "body": "For young companies that just come out to market, creating a fancy brand is one of the key problems. The elders are often facing the need to attract potential clients to get out of the competition and build a foundation for long-term development. In this process, the brands become an independent tool.\n\nThe first step to make a brand-new startup is to define mission and company values. Without a clear understanding of why you exist and what kind of problem you're solving, it's hard to create a complete brand image. You have to formulate how your product or service changes customer life to better. For example, if your startup is an ecological solution, it should be shown in everything from a colorful gamma to a communication style.\n\nThe next important thing is to create a unique visual style. Logo, colors, fonts and other graphical elements should not only be aesthetics, but also to correspond to brand character. In this matter, it's better to address professional designers to help you bring your ideas into life and create a memorable image.\n\nIn addition to the visual ingredient, a brand has to include a small of voice style and a tone of communication. It's about advertising texts and customer correspondence. For example, for a milky start, it's appropriate to use a non-formal style with humor, whereas for financial services, the official tone will fit.\n\nBy creating a brandy, it's important to consider the future development of a company. Even if your startup only starts its way, it's worth thinking about perspective. Are you planning on going to an international market? Are you going to expand the equipment? All of these factors should be predicted to remain relevant in a few years.\n\nFor a startup, a brand-new brand is not just a tool for cognition, but also a way to attract investors. A clear and professional document demonstrates the seriousness of your intention and promotes increased confidence to the company. So building a brand early stage will help not only to succeed faster, but also to provide sustainable development in the future."
